{
  "sn41.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 41.1 ",
  "sn41.1:0.2": "1. With Citta ",
  "sn41.1:0.3": "The Fetter ",
  "sn41.1:1.1": "At one time several senior mendicants were staying near Macchikāsaṇḍa in the Wild Mango Grove. ",
  "sn41.1:1.2": "Now at that time, after the meal, on return from almsround, several senior mendicants sat together in the pavilion and this discussion came up among them: ",
  "sn41.1:1.3": "“Reverends, the ‘fetter’ and the ‘things that tighten the fetters’: do these things differ in both meaning and phrasing? Or do they mean the same thing, and differ only in the phrasing?” ",
  "sn41.1:1.4": "Some senior mendicants answered like this: ",
  "sn41.1:1.5": "“Reverends, the ‘fetter’ and the ‘things that tighten the fetters’: these things differ in both meaning and phrasing.” ",
  "sn41.1:1.6": "But some senior mendicants answered like this: ",
  "sn41.1:1.7": "“Reverends, the ‘fetter’ and the ‘things that tighten the fetters’ mean the same thing; they differ only in the phrasing.” ",
  "sn41.1:2.1": "Now at that time the householder Citta had arrived at Migapathaka on some business. ",
  "sn41.1:2.2": "He heard about what those senior mendicants were discussing. ",
  "sn41.1:2.3": "",
  "sn41.1:2.4": "",
  "sn41.1:2.5": "",
  "sn41.1:2.6": "",
  "sn41.1:2.7": "",
  "sn41.1:3.1": "So he went up to them, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to them, ",
  "sn41.1:3.2": "“Sirs, I heard that you were discussing whether the ‘fetter’ and the ‘things